        {
          "kicker": "World rankings",
          "heading": "Australia miss five-year high after heavy Bledisloe Cup loss in Auckland",
          "body": "The Wallabies remain sixth in the world rugby rankings following their 50-19 defeat at Eden Park, failing to capitalise on an opportunity to reach their highest position since November 2021. Had Australia secured a victory by more than 15 points, they could have risen to fourth. Instead, the loss saw their rating points drop to 84.89, leaving them just 0.11 ahead of seventh-placed Scotland. Another defeat in next Saturday’s Bledisloe Cup rematch in Sydney would see them slip further down the table."
        },
        {
